@@ -2447,6 +2447,24 @@ renderer owns its layout. Tune that card with the `mdCode*` metrics.

 ### `<diff>`

+The 1git `diff-view` patch adds `showFileHeader` (default `true`) to remove
+native file-header rows, and `autoWidth` (default `false`) to derive the minimum
+width from GPUI-shaped visible text. Set `width: '100%'`, `flexShrink: 0` inside
+an X-only viewport to fill short diffs and scroll long ones. Measurement is
+cached per patch, collapsed/truncated row set, font and metrics; scrolling and
+color changes do not remeasure. File paths remain clipped in native headers
+and do not expand the code width. `diffRowPaddingX` also controls code padding.
+
+`theme.diffAddBg`, `diffDelBg`, `diffAddWordBg` and `diffDelWordBg` accept CSS
+colors (including alpha) independently of markers and syntax. Omitted values
+preserve the existing marker-derived washes. Hunk/notice text uses `diffTextSize`.
+These are local pinned-patch APIs, not upstream GPUIX guarantees.
+
+The 1git local patch exposes the native list through `scrollTo`, `getScrollOffset`
+and `getListScrollTop` when `scroll` is enabled, including in the test renderer.
+Set `theme.metrics.diffFileHeaderHeight: 0` to omit the built-in file chrome
+when a dedicated viewer provides its own pinned filename/comparison controls.
+
 A unified diff viewer. It **flows** with its parent by default, so a parent
 list can be the only scroller. Collapsing a file removes its rows rather than hiding
 them, so a collapsed 10k-line file costs one row.
